. so the exact number of  marbles he had was 242 which is pretty  close to 240. so 240 was a good  approximation and then when you divide  that by dividing it by 31 is a bit of a  pain and luckily we can just estimate so  we divided by 30 and we got eight and  this is another kind of aside here  notice  notice 24  24 divided by three is equal to eight  and if you if you divide 240  240 divided by 30 this is also this is  also equal to 8. so if you divide  something 10 times as large by something  10 times as large you're still going to  get the same value but either way  each of his classmates are going to get  roughly eight marbles

